dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Privileged helper socket: per-connection deadline and request size limit,
    at most 64 connections at once, bounded shutdown wait, a stale socket is
    removed only if it is a socket, the socket is created 0660, and denials and
    privileged verbs log the caller's uid and pid.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:50:00 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Audit follow-ups: [DESIRED:SPLIT] lists at most 20 scopes; the DHCP relay
    tracks at most 1024 client MACs per VLAN and 16384 in total; idle client
    sweeps run at most once a second; make rpm adds new files only under the
    source directories.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:13:45 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A remembered owner that is not serving is dropped at once when a peer's
    map at the same generation disagrees (faster handover after a restart).
  * make rpm includes untracked source files.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:43:19 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Desired-state split warning only after 45 s (beyond the 30 s grace that
    heals a restarted owner); shorter splits are logged when they heal.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:24:59 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Helper restarts a DHCP/DNS relay running a replaced binary instead of
    reloading it (RPM upgrades left the old relay running).
  * Rejoining core adopts its peers' watermark before its first desired map.
  * Cores compare desired-state maps and log a split at equal generation.
  * Every handover gap of 5 s or more is logged when it ends.
  * DHCP relay: per-VLAN pending cap, 30 s entry lifetime, per-client rate
    limit, warnings and counters, all on by default.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:14:44 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A scope no longer stays unserved after its non-preferred owner restarts:
    a remembered owner is kept only while it is seen serving the scope.
  * Unserved scopes and desired-state owner changes are logged.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:55:35 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * DHCP relay hardening: server socket swapped atomically on reload, new
    interfaces get the reload's cluster-wide rate limit, cheaper drop path,
    one clock read per request, no per-packet allocations; fuzz tests and
    benchmarks for the packet paths.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:34:32 +0200

dnshived (0.9.8.6~dev-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Core nodes verify each witness grant and renewal (PSK signature, scope,
    owner, incarnation, plausible expiry) before counting it as a vote.

 -- Andreas Dunkl <andreas@dunkl.net>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:51:11 +0200

